<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corpus Evangelicorum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1653">1653</a>–<a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Corpus Evangelicorum was the body of the Protestant estates at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-diet">Imperial Diet</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, formally constituted in 1653 under the Peace of Westphalia, which allowed religious questions to be settled by agreement between the Protestant and Catholic bodies rather than by majority vote. Its directorship stayed with the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> even after Augustus the Strong became a Catholic in 1697. It lasted until the end of the Empire in 1806.</p></div>
